I Only Danced This Pyramid Because You Asked Me To.

Ingrid, the director who only practised this dance because your static shapes were embarrassing.
Astrid, the screen column who walks beside you solely to stop you getting lost.
Sigrid, the screen row who saved you a place but insists it was an accident.
Solveig, the face counter who checks every side because you clearly cannot manage alone.
Nora, the number of frames shown and certainly not the number of times she thought of you.
Liv, the glyph who rehearsed her lines but definitely not for your approval.
Eira, the cosine who keeps her distance whenever you catch her smiling.
Frida, the sine who turns toward you and pretends it was a coincidence.
Maja, the nearest surface who only came closer because you looked lonely.
Thea, the farthest surface who keeps her distance whenever you catch her smiling.
Hedda, the plane slope who says your perspective needs adult supervision.
Sunniva, the plane intercept who brought an extra scarf but claims she hates waste.
Runa, the candidate depth who tells you to stop staring.
Tuva, the scratch calculation who will help but only this once.
Hanne, the visible face who is definitely not blushing.
Vilde, the brightness who shines for geometry and not for your smile.
Kari, the requested frame count who says zero means she can stay as long as she likes.
Marit, the skipped frames who waited for you and denies that it meant anything.
Oda, the rotation phase who counts sixty four steps and calls it mere practice.
Tove, the horizontal sway who only follows you because this is her route too.
Ylva, the vertical bob who will not admit she is excited to see you.
Hilde, the translated horizontal coordinate who only moved over to make room.
Silje, the translated vertical coordinate who keeps your seat warm for no reason at all.
Anja, the first plane slope who practised her angle but not for your sake.
Bente, the second plane slope who insists she just happened to turn up.
Grete, the third plane slope who corrects your posture and calls it charity.
Heidi, the fourth plane slope who only stayed because leaving would be rude.
Inger, the first plane offset who moves over and denies saving you room.
Lene, the second plane offset who says teamwork does not mean she likes you.
Mette, the shared plane offset who keeps everyone together for purely practical reasons.

